#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133563 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca46ab2-488a-5596-b96b-559463731556" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Images of the Standard Basis Vectors Under a Given Linear Transformation"}] :question/id #uuid "4748324b-8edf-5fba-90e1-90683887d463" :question/math-academy-id "e-5436" :question/problem "The linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ has the standard matrix \n![](images/6a/6a14933078db8802426a1ab22ba692e17fd6f795ec4bd746a6fb16687aa441ed.svg) \nWhat are the images of the standard basis vectors $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j} \\}$ of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ under the action of $\\mathbf T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j} \\}$ are the first and second columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j} \\}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot\\mathbf{i}$ and $T\\cdot\\mathbf{j}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133564 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2845913-5c76-57f5-a4d3-139a6513225b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "0db64243-ffa4-595b-8555-5ee369450557" :question/math-academy-id "e-5437" :question/problem "In the diagram below, $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf j$ are the vectors of the standard basis of $\\mathbb{R}^2$, while $\\mathbf{i'}$ and $\\mathbf{j'}$ are their images under the linear transformation $\\mathbf T.$\nWhat is the standard matrix of $\\mathbf T?$\n\n![](images/4d/4d1b9e56c0c6214d949d12f45fe4aecea5516971203724ecf573a2b17c6e959a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nFrom the diagram we see that\n\n- the image of $\\mathbf{i}$ is ![](images/95/95f30188b01782a32f4dbfdf48aae31e06846b0faa4a6f741e921ad64910221b.svg) and\n\n- the image of $\\mathbf{j}$ is ![](images/0f/0f695a9b9d87ca060eb5011b616d77b7e7d8d9394de6d537a2f2aab759c26a86.svg)\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n![](images/a2/a28158d8b163a3ec2ef4c568f7a4bbc63cf8b89385117a1e6178193d7cba886a.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133565 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b057dd5e-f80e-5d3f-84ae-b6aebd5800ea" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Image of the Standard Basis"}] :question/id #uuid "ae7884f7-abb9-56ba-b685-f0eab27ff795" :question/math-academy-id "e-5438" :question/problem "Given that $\\{ \\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j}, \\mathbf k\\}$ is the standard basis of $\\mathbb{R}^3$ and the images of $\\mathbf{i},$ $\\mathbf{j},$ and $\\mathbf{k}$ under the action of a linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ are\n$\\langle 3, 5, -1 \\rangle,$ $\\langle 0, 4,3 \\rangle,$ and $\\langle -1, 5, -2\\rangle,$ respectively, what is the standard matrix of $\\mathbf{T}?$" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in $\\mathbb{R}^3$ can be represented as a $3\\times 3$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $\\mathbf{i}, \\mathbf{j},$ and $\\mathbf k$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n![](images/93/93176243866490c0c75a41aae16977e257bf0f3aae91d91f36edd6408a2c6ab7.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271994 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b057dd5e-f80e-5d3f-84ae-b6aebd5800ea" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Image of the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b0019e2-cffc-5750-82e8-690b958a87b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -8 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269806} {:answer/id #uuid "430f7130-acca-583f-ab0b-5ca3f66be3bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269874} {:answer/id #uuid "8546e3f0-cba7-51d3-a1ee-ce0cf743a1c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270420} {:answer/id #uuid "8ac36670-0795-5825-a9a1-9790464f6b5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270469} {:answer/id #uuid "93efc544-d266-5b7e-8bf4-1dbe6c3c7929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93efc544-d266-5b7e-8bf4-1dbe6c3c7929" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270563} :answer-field/id #uuid "9211e17c-0252-57c3-accc-d22b89c4a0f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2acd8b1-57b0-5fbb-ab92-5d2e7cadb54d" :question/math-academy-id "q-139988" :question/problem "Given that ${i,j}$ is the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ and that the images of $i$ and $j$ under the action of a linear transformation $T$ are $⟨-1,2⟩$ and $⟨3,-8⟩$, respectively, what is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{2}$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186476902 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca46ab2-488a-5596-b96b-559463731556" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Images of the Standard Basis Vectors Under a Given Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ae34b84-cdf9-5084-96a7-e1064e0ede3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ $[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ and  $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476255} {:answer/id #uuid "b22a7780-0481-512f-919f-1c5bb88142ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and  $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476602} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d632c2-ccae-5246-8658-c6353980158b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and  $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476676} {:answer/id #uuid "d70c60d2-7d41-5ba2-9b01-cb02f8562fb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and  $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476687} {:answer/id #uuid "fd2ef2e8-1704-5aeb-bbc6-24028bb553e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ $[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ and  $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b22a7780-0481-512f-919f-1c5bb88142ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and  $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476602} :answer-field/id #uuid "d76409e5-f891-5850-b69c-49a2c2e9eb94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ebff972-8ab2-5583-88cb-dd4e3c35dfe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-139994" :question/problem "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors $\\{i,j,k\\}$ of ${R}^{3}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j,k\\}$ are the first, second, and third columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j,k\\}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i,$ $T\\cdot j,$ and $T\\cdot k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(k) & =T\\cdot k=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2845913-5c76-57f5-a4d3-139a6513225b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fd796e3-143b-5855-aea6-138f016b5e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476273} {:answer/id #uuid "7e8d4d90-3061-5a98-a843-cf7ecb939b1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476483} {:answer/id #uuid "8776d28a-e6e4-5e00-bae7-b7f29525627b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476499} {:answer/id #uuid "aa6028ab-7d73-547f-836e-0a3ea3e0c540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476579} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1d48b7-4ef8-5718-acb3-8d366a9ecbcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fd796e3-143b-5855-aea6-138f016b5e7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476273} :answer-field/id #uuid "384786b2-da5d-5687-8efa-cabf3fb09792" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d45923a4-c5c5-54fb-9905-415ac3f45f69" :question/math-academy-id "q-43837" :question/problem "![](images/ad/ad1f032fd5b99252d348d0cf71308ef1de0f65f06ddd9070b569cff69bc506f9.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $i$ and $j$ are the vectors of the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$, while ${i}^{′}$ and ${j}^{′}$ are their images under the linear transformation $T.$\nWhat is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{2}$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nFrom the diagram we see that \n${i}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ \nand \n${j}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134430 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca46ab2-488a-5596-b96b-559463731556" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Images of the Standard Basis Vectors Under a Given Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38025c76-7296-51ce-b26c-f8e7311afc56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476328} {:answer/id #uuid "51d82f90-9a22-5286-ad37-3dac355225c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476376} {:answer/id #uuid "6fbe14ec-f5b8-5b17-b0f7-8b51c052798d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476452} {:answer/id #uuid "c167f295-c000-56a8-a353-b451577aa310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476640} {:answer/id #uuid "e498fa1c-b1fb-500f-a040-f84da4313219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e498fa1c-b1fb-500f-a040-f84da4313219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186476711} :answer-field/id #uuid "086168dd-27ed-5da8-8056-ad16a2b501b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "655dd154-95c9-5f77-bf5c-6a9ca9818844" :question/math-academy-id "q-43893" :question/problem "The linear transformation $T$ has the standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nWhat are the respective images of the standard basis vectors $\\{i,j\\}$ of ${R}^{2}$ under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nThe images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j\\}$ are the first and second columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis $\\{i,j\\}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i$ and $T\\cdot j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134431 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2845913-5c76-57f5-a4d3-139a6513225b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "128d12cf-7219-571f-8604-72f6081e98b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327092} {:answer/id #uuid "2d63549e-9e03-5e43-91c0-e0bebfca9523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327335} {:answer/id #uuid "648c3142-a08d-5678-9c36-e4b94e3fae26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327808} {:answer/id #uuid "92ca9032-6c4b-556b-b7e8-0beca5199ae9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328213} {:answer/id #uuid "c891ed12-3192-58b6-a08a-57887d4a2173" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d63549e-9e03-5e43-91c0-e0bebfca9523" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327335} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed0d78f6-594b-587e-a24e-7ac269c126cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329598}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e98d2b13-3a52-5439-8add-029a6bea2d0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-43894" :question/problem "![](images/5a/5aaf29ab4dd2de3d104ca37a71ee66078f985b908465a77ca06ba8ffadd50210.png)\n\nIn the diagram above,  $i$ and $j$ are the vectors of the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$, while ${i}^{′}$ and  ${j}^{′}$ are their images under the linear transformation $T.$\nWhat is the standard matrix of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{2}$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nFrom the diagram we see that \n${i}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ \nand \n${j}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b057dd5e-f80e-5d3f-84ae-b6aebd5800ea" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Standard Matrix of a Linear Transformation Given the Image of the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "262e6574-f0a8-5e20-9194-efcddae60ce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342563} {:answer/id #uuid "7022cab5-c16f-59e8-8443-f646f2928c72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343201} {:answer/id #uuid "83ed0187-3fcb-58e8-872c-d75f939d004a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498